## About the Project

**Grama Khata** is an Android application that digitizes the traditional credit management system used by small village shopkeepers in rural Karnataka. It replaces physical "Vahi" (credit books) with a simple, offline-first digital ledger.

> Project 68 | Android App Development using GenAI
> Mindmatrix Pro Internship Program

---

## Problem Statement

Small grocery stores in villages still use physical "Vahi" books to track customer credit. When these books get damaged or lost, it causes:
- Financial loss and disputes between shopkeeper and customer
- No automated balance calculation (manual errors)
- No reminder system for pending dues
- No daily business summary

---

## Solution

Grama Khata provides:
- Simple Give/Take interface (Koduvudu / Tegedukolluvudu)
- Offline-first storage using Room Database
- Real-time net balance calculation
- AI-generated daily collection reports via Google Gemini
- One-tap WhatsApp payment reminders

---

## Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| Customer Management | Add, search, delete customers with initials avatar |
| Transaction Logging | Simple + (PAID) and - (DUE) buttons |
| Real-time Balance | Net balance updates instantly after every transaction |
| Due Dashboard | All customers sorted by highest amount owed |
| AI Daily Report | Gemini AI generates collection summary |
| WhatsApp Reminder | AI-generated polite message sent via WhatsApp |
| Offline First | Works fully without internet for all core features |

